        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "rational inequality",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (245) an inequality that consists of one or more rational expressions "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "ratio test",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (785) a method to test convergence in an infinite series "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "real part of a complex number",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (581) a in the complex number a \u0003 bi "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "rectangular form",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (581) a complex number written as x \u0003 yi, where x is the real part and yi is the imaginary part "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "rectangular hyperbola",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (648) A special case of the equilateral hyperbola, where the coordinate axes are the asymptotes. The general equation of a rectangular hyperbola is xy \u0001 c, where c is a nonzero constant. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "recursive formula",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (758) a formula used for determining the next term of a sequence using one or more of the previous terms "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "reduced sample space",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (862) the subset of a sample space that contains only those outcomes that satisfy a given condition "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "reduction identity",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (446) identity that involves adding and subtracting the quandrantal angles, 90°, 180°, and 270°, from the angle measure to find equivalent values of a trigonometric function "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "reference angle",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (280) the acute angle formed by the terminal side of an angle in standard position and the x-axis "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "reflection",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (88) a linear transformation that flips a figure over a line called the line of symmetry "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "reflection matrix",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (89) a matrix used to reflect an object over a line or plane "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "regression line",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (40) a best-fit line "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "relation",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (5) a set of ordered pairs "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "relative extremum",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (172) a point that represents the maximum or minimum for a certain interval "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "relative maximum",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (172) a point that represents the maximum for a certain interval "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "relative minimum",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (172) a point that represents the minimum for a certain interval "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "resultant of vectors",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (486) the sum of two or more vectors "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": "root",
            "styles": [
              "bold"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "content": " (206) a solution of the equation P(x) \u0001 0 "
